        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "What is the fat-burning zone, and should I train in it?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "At lower intensities a higher proportion of energy comes from fat, but you use less energy overall, so the absolute amount is often similar to a harder session. The percentage is real; the conclusion is not. Train at lower intensity because you can do it more often and for longer — that is the actual benefit.",
          },
        },
