        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">Walk at an incline, often, for a long time.</strong> The
            approach with the best ratio of benefit to sustainability beats anything cleverer you
            stop doing — and consistency over twelve weeks beats intensity over three every time.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Ignore the calorie readout as accounting, add resistance training twice a week, and take
            nutrition questions to a registered dietitian rather than a treadmill site. Judge the
            first three months by whether the sessions happened, and remember the
            <a href="/treadmill-workouts/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">health benefits arrive</a>
            whether or not the scale moves.
          </p>
